WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.860
Christmas!

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.180
Concert!

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:08.950
Christmas morning in Green Gables
broke on a beautiful white world.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.870
Merry Christmas, Snow Queen!

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.600
Merry Christmas, birdies!

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.080
Merry Christmas, Marilla!

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.690
Merry Christmas.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:20.740
Merry Christmas, Matthew!

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.100
Merry Christmas, Anne.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.010
Actually, I...

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.140
Isn't it a lovely Christmas?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.760
I'm so glad it's white.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.430
The weather has been very mild so I feared
we would have a green Christmas.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:38.310
But a green Christmas
doesn't seem real, does it?

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.040
I don't like green Christmases.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.210
They're not green.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:47.040
They're just nasty faded browns and grays.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.250
What makes people call them green?

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.370
A-actually...

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.180
Oh...?

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:54.920
Matthew...!

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.960
T-this is... for you.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.970
Is that... for me?

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:15.660
This is... a Christmas present for you.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.140
Oh, Matthew!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:46.190
Why... why Anne...

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:49.520
Don't you like it?

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.550
Well now--well now.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.390
Like it!

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.940
Oh, Matthew!

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.420
It's perfectly exquisite.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.690
Oh, I can never thank you enough.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:11.540
Look at those sleeves!

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.560
Oh, it seems to me
this must be a happy dream.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.080
If this goes on the new clothes
shall be dampened with tears.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:27.340
Since Matthew has got it
for you, see that you take good care of it.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:33.320
There's a hair ribbon Mrs.
Lynde left for you.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:34.690
Mrs. Lynde?

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.710
Oh, it's brown, to match the dress.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.530
Matthew, can I go try them on?

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:50.150
Well now, I would like to see you in them too.

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:54.110
I feel like I'm in heaven!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.100
Matthew, I'll get changed quickly!

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:01.170
Anne, shouldn't you have breakfast first?

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:03.050
The tea is getting cold.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.400
You sit down too, Matthew.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.900
You're right...

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:13.100
I'm all right,  Marilla.
I don't see how I'm going to eat breakfast.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:15.830
The dress won't sprout wings and fly away.

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:22.990
Breakfast seems so commonplace
at such an exciting moment.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:27.550
I'd rather
feast my eyes on this dress.

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.750
You may feast your eyes,

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:33.310
but you have a concert today.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:35.800
If you don't eat anything,

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:37.660
you won't have the strength to perform.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:44.030
When that happens, don't mourn to me
if your noises fail to impress the others.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:58.170
Oh, It did seem to me that I'd never
get over it if puffed sleeves went out

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.770
before I had a dress with them.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:02.160
I'd never have felt quite satisfied, you see.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:08.090
I'm so glad that puffed
sleeves are still fashionable.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:12.180
It was lovely of Mrs. Lynde
to give me the ribbon too.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:17.540
It's at times like this I'm
sorry I'm not a model little girl.

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:21.400
And I always resolve that I will be in future.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:27.370
But somehow it's hard to carry out your
resolutions when irresistible temptations come.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.240
Still, I really will make an extra effort after this.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:42.270
Oh, this will be a day I'll never forget,

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:44.520
the day I wore puffed sleeves.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.690
I will always remember it.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.080
And it is as if had snow just for me!

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:53.310
It's Diana!

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.930
It's Diana! Diana is coming!

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:00.100
Really...

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.400
Diana!

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.320
Anne!

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.100
Merry Christmas, Diana!

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:15.770
Merry Christmas, Anne!

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:19.860
Diana, it's a wonderful Christmas!

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:22.520
I've something splendid to show you.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:24.000
Can you guess what it is?

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:27.700
Matthew has given me the loveliest dress,

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:29.950
with SUCH sleeves.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:33.300
I couldn't even imagine any nicer.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.650
I've got something more for you.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:36.370
What?

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.710
Here, this box.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:43.170
Aunt Josephine sent us out a big
box with ever so many things in it.

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:45.010
And this is for you.

00:08:45.430 --> 00:08:47.590
Miss Josephine sent it for me?

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.440
Yes, open it up.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:57.720
Oh!

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:03.180
Diana, this is too much.
I must be dreaming.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.920
I call it providential.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:12.080
Now you won't have to borrow Ruby's
slippers and stuff a handkerchief into them.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:15.640
Oh, Diana, did you tell Miss Josephine?

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:20.460
Anne, I'm sure Josie Pye will be delighted
to see you moving like a fairy.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.240
Thank you, Diana!

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:25.140
But it looks like I'm dreaming!

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:28.020
Diana, could you pinch me?

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:29.960
All right.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:31.500
Here goes.

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:36.320
What will I do, Diana?

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:37.280
What's wrong?

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.830
It didn't hurt!

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.460
It really must be a dream!

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:45.170
Of course. I only pretended to pinch you.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:47.510
Diana, really!

00:10:56.930 --> 00:10:58.750
Well? How do I look?

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.600
What do you think, Matthew?

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:02.920
W-well now,

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:06.080
I think it fits snugly.

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:12.690
For this dress, I shall work hard tonight.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:14.690
Thank you, Matthew!

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:18.220
N-no... I just...

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:19.610
Oh no!

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.950
Diana is waiting for me. I have to run!

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:28.050
We have to go early to decorate the hall.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:31.340
I know! When I return I won't
just tell you about the concert.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:36.280
I will also recite for
Matthew while wearing this dress.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:38.630
No... Well... I...

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:40.570
Would you like to hear it too, Marilla?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.780
I'm sorry, but I will have to refuse.

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:45.250
Why?

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:46.650
Does your head hurt?

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:51.890
Because it will be enough to listen
to your groans in the concert tonight.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:55.390
Marilla, you...

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.890
My, why are you two so surprised?

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:02.780
Because you were so against the concert,

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:06.950
I thought you weren't interested to go.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:13.270
Really, of course I will support
a concert organized by the school.

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.490
Marilla...

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:17.910
Well, if you keep wasting time,
you will keep Diana waiting.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:19.480
I can't do that! I have to hurry!

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:21.220
Well...

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:23.070
Marilla, the concert starts at...

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:23.280
At 6 pm, I know.
Marilla, the concert starts at...

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:24.960
At 6 pm, I know.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.700
Anne, actually I...

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.190
Don't worry, Matthew.

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:35.010
If my ankle begins to hurt
during the performance,

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:40.750
I'll just think about this dress
and I'm sure I'll get better.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:43.350
Matthew, Marilla, I'm going.

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:47.040
I-I'll...

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.680
I will go too.

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:53.380
What? What did you just say, Matthew?

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:56.900
Well... I will go too.

00:12:57.190 --> 00:12:58.850
You are going?

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.460
I definitely will.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:06.490
What is going on?
You are going for a concert?

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:13.080
I just... well... I just decided to go now.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:35.230
All the Avonlea scholars were
in a fever of excitement that day.

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:41.580
The hall had to be decorated
and a last grand rehearsal held.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.650
The little hall was crowded.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:53.400
At 6 pm, the Christmas concert
held by the Avonlea scholars, began.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.570
After 2 months of practice,
the performances were exciting.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:17.620
For first timers all have done very well.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:24.540
The Christmas performances of the students
gained the warm reception of the audience.

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:46.840
But, Diana's solo was the best
one of the first part of the program.

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:50.690
Diana's solo captured the audience's heart
and they kept calling for an encore.

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:56.740
And of course, Anne was
happier than any other for that.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:01.060
Matthew?

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:16.310
Anne, it's your turn.

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:41.320
This life and corpse has no difference,
Its eyes see and sees not,

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:44.720
Wretched soul which strives to survive,

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:48.330
The remorseful self keeps on like this,

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.370
Borrowed into death's representation,

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.060
Now I...

00:16:52.060 --> 00:16:56.920
When she saw that the person she
most wished to be there was present,

00:16:56.930 --> 00:17:03.160
Anne gave her whole heart
and soul into her act.

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:08.510
My accursed destiny!

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:14.830
Oh, please give me a gravestone.
Give me a dark dwelling.

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:21.240
Then keep my bones there,
thus letting my body lie in peace...

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:37.150
Anne's sad recital...

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:42.880
...brought down the house with applause.

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:48.290
In the heated performances,
Christmas night slowly descended.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:52.860
That night, each group did different plays.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:58.610
Although Anne and Josie Pye
didn't have a fairylike appearance,

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:01.780
the Fairy Queen was the best one of them.

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:05.360
Oh! Your face is full of splendor.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:10.060
You brighten the earth like rays of sunlight.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:12.050
And you gentle heart...

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:23.420
...is loved and respected by everyone.
Fairy Queen...

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:27.790
...today is your birthday.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:33.300
Your servants will hold a grand banquet
to celebrate this day.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:38.620
Fairy Queen, I have a request for you.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:42.870
Then speak out your request.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:46.100
Lately in our village of Avonlea...

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:49.790
Under peals of tremendous laughter,

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:53.820
Anne and the other girls
finished the Fairy Queen play,

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:56.360
and while leaving the stage,
something minute happened.

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:02.920
Of course, not too many knew about it.

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:21.990
Farewell to the deep valleys
covered with beautiful snow.

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:26.350
Farewell to the lush green slopes.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:30.800
Farewell to the forest of no dwellers.

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:35.020
Farewell to the fast streams of water.

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:38.000
My heart belongs to the mountains,

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:39.430
my heart doesn't belong here.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:43.580
My heart is hunting deers in the high peaks.

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:46.490
Pursuing wild deers.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:51.780
No matter where I go, my heart
will always be in the mountains.

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:09.070
The first Christmas concert held
by the Avonlea school students

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:14.770
was a success thanks to their
hard work and passion.

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:18.540
Oh, hasn't it been a brilliant evening?

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:22.400
Everything went off very well.
I think we made at least ten dollars.

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:24.790
Then it should be enough for the flag.

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:31.190
Yes. Mr. Allan is going to send an account
of it to the Charlottetown papers.

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:32.510
Really?

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:38.300
Will we really see our names in print?
It makes me thrill to think of it.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:44.540
Your solo was perfectly elegant. I felt
prouder than you did when it was encored.

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:50.140
I just said to myself, 'It is my dear
bosom friend who is so honored'.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:54.000
Well, your recitations just
brought down the house, Anne.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:57.390
Oh, I was so nervous.

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:01.170
My voice seemed to be
coming from ever so far away.

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:03.210
Did I groan all right?

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.950
You groaned lovely.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:08.230
I saw old Mrs. Sloane wiping away tears.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:12.820
Oh, I'll never forget the
splendid emotion I felt today.

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:15.340
Gilbert Blythe was just splendid.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:18.190
I do think it's awful
mean the way you treat Gil.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.760
Please don't say that to me, Diana.

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:23.160
That night...

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:27.170
Marilla and Matthew, who had been out
to a concert for the first time in twenty years,

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:31.800
sat for a while by the kitchen fire after
Anne had gone to bed.

00:21:34.200 --> 00:21:40.000
Well now, I guess our
Anne did as well as any of them.

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:41.390
Yes, she did.

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:44.240
She's a bright child, Matthew.

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:47.710
And she looked real nice too.

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:52.540
I've been kind of opposed
to this concert scheme, but...

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:56.300
Anyhow, I was proud of Anne tonight,

00:21:56.780 --> 00:22:00.240
although I'm not going to tell her so.

00:22:00.370 --> 00:22:08.010
Well now, I was proud of her and I
did tell her so 'fore she went upstairs.

00:22:16.720 --> 00:22:23.260
We must see what we can
do for her some of these days, Marilla.

00:22:23.990 --> 00:22:26.050
What do you mean by that?

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:32.890
I guess she'll need something
more than Avonlea school by and by.

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:35.420
There's time enough to think of that.

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:39.290
She's only thirteen in March.

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:44.270
Though tonight it struck me
she was growing quite a big girl.

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:46.310
Right.

00:22:46.850 --> 00:22:50.090
Girls need to dress up a little.

00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:58.880
That's right. She's quick to learn.

00:22:58.880 --> 00:23:04.640
I guess the best thing we can do
for her will be to send her to Queen's.

00:23:05.030 --> 00:23:08.350
Queen's Academy. You're right.

00:23:09.130 --> 00:23:13.570
But nothing need be said about that
for a year or two yet.

00:23:14.640 --> 00:23:20.170
Well now, it'll do no harm to
be thinking it over off and on.

00:23:20.170 --> 00:23:26.050
Things like that are all the better
for lots of thinking over.

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:30.410
She's been here for only two years

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:33.760
and yet we already have to be
thinking about parting with her.

00:23:33.770 --> 00:23:35.620
Yes.

00:24:18.150 --> 00:24:21.820
After the concert,
Avonlea goes back to normal

00:24:21.820 --> 00:24:25.270
and Anne and Diana start a new club.

00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:28.400
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:30.720
Anne's Story Club Is Formed

00:24:30.720 --> 00:24:31.300
Please watch!
